        "Finding Valerie’s emotional journey was one of the most challenging parts of directing the play. I wanted to understand how she could finally say “I love you” and still be filled with pain and struggle. I spoke at length with the actor playing Valerie, and we watched several films that explored similar themes. Through those conversations, we reached a shared understanding: Valerie was not simply refusing to face her feelings. She was not ready to face them within the pressures of family expectations, school relationships, and the wider social environment around her. This distinction changed how we approached her. Rather than playing her as someone who needed to overcome denial, the actor could show a young person trying to understand herself while managing the fear of what that understanding might cost. Her final confession was therefore not a sudden transformation into certainty, but a difficult act of honesty.",
